{
 "command": "dialog-zoom-diagnostics",
 "notes": [
  "Feeds W8-18p (dialogs::{zoom_prompt, diagnostics}). Reflection over the internal ZoomPromptDialog and DiagnosticsDialog of the PhotoReview (Shell.Win32) assembly and the internal DiagnosticsDisplay of PhotoReview.App.Shared; no window is created. The language is the process default (English), so the texts are the English catalog values.",
  "Output per kind: zoom_dialog -> title, items [{class, id, text, style, ex_style}], initial_focus_id, default_button_id, resizable, header_ids, uses_modal_frame, extra_window_style, initial_text; diagnostics_dialog -> the same without initial_text; diagnostics_text -> labels[15], values[15], copy_text; diagnostics_row -> label and value, or threw (exception type name); preferred -> preferred_width, preferred_height, minimum_width, minimum_height; constants -> zoom_label_id, zoom_edit_id, zoom_error_id, zoom_cancel_id, zoom_apply_id, diagnostics_header_id, diagnostics_note_id, diagnostics_first_label_id, diagnostics_first_value_id, diagnostics_copy_id, diagnostics_close_id, diagnostics_row_count.",
  "preferred: a window-less dialog (RuntimeHelpers.GetUninitializedObject with _avgCharWidth, _lineHeight, _childHosts set; zoom also _errorVisible), so every MeasureItemHeight is 0 and ButtonWidth is exactly Dx(50). It pins the dialog-unit arithmetic of PreferredClientSize and MinimumClientSize; the wrapped-text heights are hand-checked in the Rust tests with a fake measure.",
  "display is the 15 strings of DiagnosticsDisplay in declaration order (CacheHits, CacheMisses, HitRate, SourceBytes, SourceReads, DecodeTime, PresentLatency, ExplorerOrder, ExplorerMetadata, SourceOpens, StatCount, SessionWrites, DecoderFallbacks, PresentHistogram, CrossThreadPresents). The odd display holds an empty string, a tab and a line break to show that BuildCopyText does not escape anything."
 ],
